# Lesson 2, from the point-count exercise hand 4, as responder to 2NT.
title: Partner opens 2NT, you have 3
id: L02-13
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.4
student: S
board: 13
dealer: N
vulnerable: both

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  KJ4    AKQ97  43     AKQ
  E  76532  86     AKT2   T5
  S  Q8     JT43   865    9642
  W  AT9    52     QJ97   J873

auction:
  N 2NT    = 21-22 points, balanced
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = Fewer than 4 points
     key: 3 HCP. Opposite 21-22, your side has 25 at most, and usually less. Pass.
     not 3NT: Did you count 3? A raise to 3NT needs 4 or more.
     not *: With fewer than 4 points opposite 2NT, the lesson says pass.
  W Pass

auction recap:
  Partner's 2NT showed 21-22 points and a balanced hand. With fewer than 4
  points, your side is very likely short of the 25 needed for game, so you
  pass. North is declarer, because he bid no-trump first, and so East will
  lead to the first trick.

play:
  1   E DK  S D5  W DQ  N D3
  2   E D2  S D6  W DJ  N D4
  3   W D9  N S4  E DA  S D8
  4   E DT  S C2  W D7  N SJ
  5   E S2  S S8  W SA  N SK
  6   W ST  N H7  E S3  S SQ
      note: Dummy's ♠Q wins.
  7   S HJ  W H2  N H9  E H6
      note: Declarer's plan: run the hearts and clubs. Start the hearts from dummy while you're there.
  8   S H3  W H5  N HQ  E H8
      note: Over to declarer's ♥Q.
  9   N HA  E S5  S H4  W C3
      note: More hearts.
  10  N HK  E S6  S HT  W C7
      note: The ♥K.
  11  N CQ  E C5  S C4  W C8
      note: Now the clubs.
  12  N CK  E CT  S C6  W CJ
      note: Keep going.
  13  N CA  E S7  S C9  W S9
      note: The last club. 8 tricks: 2NT made.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: hope the defenders' diamonds split evenly, then take
  the heart and club winners.

  2NT made exactly. Your four hearts helped partner run the suit, but with
  only 3 points, passing was right.
